JUDGMENT
REFUTED: the direct projector accepts expiresAt, but the actual single and batch manager paths omit the resolved expiresAt when reconstructing CanonicalEvent for projection. Both derived and explicit expiry survive on events yet are absent from chunks.
The TTL index definition itself is correct and pinned: key expiresAt ascending, expireAfterSeconds 0, partial exists true.
Conversation search filters are guarded, but bridge search filters are separate and unguarded; direct chunk locator reads are also not consumers of buildConversationChunkFilter.
Documentation accurately states the intended shipped behavior, but the implementation counterexample makes that statement false. Under warning-now-moot interpretation no warning is needed only after propagation actually works; under must-still-warn interpretation there is no warning. Under either interpretation, current docs do not disclose the live retention gap.
